From: chasey-dev <ellenyoung0912@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mt_wifi: build CFG80211_LostApInform for STA-only builds

RT_CFG80211_LOST_AP_INFORM() is defined when CONFIG_STA_SUPPORT is set,
either alone or together with APCLI_CFG80211_SUPPORT, and it is used from
sta_mgmt_cntl.c.  The definition of the target function lives in
cfg80211_apcli.c, which is wrapped as a whole in #ifdef
APCLI_CFG80211_SUPPORT, so a build with STA support but without APCLI
support compiled the two callers and no definition:

    ERROR: modpost: "CFG80211_LostApInform" [mt_wifi.ko] undefined!

The body only touches StaCfg[0] and the cfg80211 STA state, so it is valid
outside the APCLI guard.  Close the file-wide guard just for this function
and re-open it afterwards, which keeps the APCLI code paths unchanged and
also keeps the function available when APCLI support is enabled.

Signed-off-by: chasey-dev <ellenyoung0912@gmail.com>
---
--- a/mt_wifi/os/linux/cfg80211/cfg80211_apcli.c
+++ b/mt_wifi/os/linux/cfg80211/cfg80211_apcli.c
@@ -92,6 +92,13 @@
 }
 
 
+#endif /* APCLI_CFG80211_SUPPORT */
+
+/*
+ * ponwrt: this is the STA-mode half of the lost-AP notification. The caller
+ * (RT_CFG80211_LOST_AP_INFORM) is enabled by CONFIG_STA_SUPPORT as well, so
+ * the definition must be available without APCLI_CFG80211_SUPPORT.
+ */
 VOID CFG80211_LostApInform(VOID *pAdOrg)
 {
 	PRTMP_ADAPTER pAd = (PRTMP_ADAPTER)pAdOrg;
@@ -122,6 +129,8 @@
 	}
 }
 
+#ifdef APCLI_CFG80211_SUPPORT
+
 VOID CFG80211DRV_ApClientKeyAdd(VOID *pAdOrg, VOID *pData)
 {
 	PRTMP_ADAPTER pAd = (PRTMP_ADAPTER)pAdOrg;
